  "releaseNotes": "MimeKit 5.0 is a major release containing a number of breaking changes. See https://github.com/jstedfast/MimeKit/blob/master/ReleaseNotes.md for the complete list of changes and migration notes.\n\n* MimeKit.Cryptography contains the S/MIME, PGP/MIME, DKIM, ARC and DMARC support that was previously part of MimeKit. Call CryptographyModule.Initialize () during startup, and add a using MimeKit.Cryptography; directive for the MimeMessage.Sign (), Encrypt () and SignAndEncrypt () extension methods.\n* Visitors that handle signed or encrypted entities must now derive from CryptographicMimeVisitor.\n* CryptographyContext no longer registers a default S/MIME context. Applications must explicitly register the context they want. This makes MimeKit AOT-compatible.\n* Added DmarcVerifier and DmarcRecord for DMARC validation.\n* Replaced IDkimPublicKeyLocator with the more general IDnsResolver interface, and DKIM key records are now parsed more strictly per RFC 6376.\n* DkimVerifier.Verify () now returns a DkimSignatureValidationResult describing why a signature did not pass, and ArcVerifier.Verify () now provides diagnostics for ARC chain validation failures.\n* MimeMessage.Sign () and SignAndEncrypt () overloads that do not take a DigestAlgorithm now use SHA-256 instead of SHA-1.\n* Moved the digest algorithm preference APIs from CryptographyContext to OpenPgpContext.\n* Removed previously obsoleted APIs, including the obsolete DkimSigner, ArcSigner and IX509CertificateDatabase APIs.",
